## Repository files navigation
A Neovim AI coding assistant for coding with LLMs (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Copilot and [more](https://codecompanion.olimorris.dev/getting-started.html)) and AI agents.

## ✨ Features
- 💬 [Copilot Chat](https://github.com/features/copilot) meets [Zed AI](https://zed.dev/blog/zed-ai), in Neovim

## 🧰 Troubleshooting
```
-- lazy.nvim
{
  "olimorris/codecompanion.nvim",
  dependencies = {
    "nvim-lua/plenary.nvim",
    "nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter",
  },
  opts = {
    -- NOTE: The log_level is in `opts.opts`
    opts = {
      log_level = "DEBUG", -- or "TRACE"
    },
  },
},

-- Other package managers
require("codecompanion").setup({
  opts = {
    log_level = "DEBUG", -- or "TRACE"
  }
})
```

# avante.nvim vs CodeCompanion - AI Inside Neovim in 2026
( [tag: neovim](https://samuellawrentz.com/blog/tag/neovim/), [tag: ai](https://samuellawrentz.com/blog/tag/ai/), [tag: vim](https://samuellawrentz.com/blog/tag/vim/), [tag: productivity](https://samuellawrentz.com/blog/tag/productivity/))

Two plugins dominate the Neovim AI space in 2026: [avante.nvim](https://github.com/yetone/avante.nvim) (17K+ stars, Cursor-style AI) and [CodeCompanion.nvim](https://github.com/olimorris/codecompanion.nvim) (6K+ stars, buffer-integrated AI).

## What They’re Actually Doing
**CodeCompanion** feels woven into Neovim itself.

## Setup, Minimal
```
{
  "yetone/avante.nvim",
  opts = {
    provider = "claude",
    claude = { model = "claude-sonnet-4-5" },
  }
}
```

**CodeCompanion**:

```
{
  "olimorris/codecompanion.nvim",
  opts = {
    adapters = {
      anthropic = require("codecompanion.adapters").extend("anthropic", {
        schema = { model = { default = "claude-sonnet-4-5" } }
      })
    },
    strategies = {
      chat = { adapter = "anthropic" },
      inline = { adapter = "anthropic" }
    }
  }
}
```

## My Pick
If you only install one: **CodeCompanion**.
